{"toolCallId":"call_69ab690764fa4219845de9bc5e8c3c62","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"--- spec.md ---\n100:| REQ-009 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr: `--quiet` trims stdout only and never the diagnostics channel |\n--- tasks.md ---\n84:- [ ] T017 Keep the quiet path off fd 2: `output_quiet()` writes only to stdout and adds no stderr redirection, so a warning the script writes to stderr still reaches stderr under `--quiet` (REQ-009) (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -A6 '^output_quiet\\(\\)' \"$S\"` prints the function body with no `>&2` or `2>` line, and `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc abc --files 3 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`.\n--- acceptance ---\n65:| AC-010 | REQ-009 | Given a `--quiet` run whose path writes a warning to stderr, When the script runs, Then the warning is still written to stderr and stdout holds only the level line | `rg -n -A6 '^output_quiet\\(\\)' \"$S\"` shows no `>&2` or `2>` line in the quiet function, and `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc abc --files 3 2>&1 >/dev/null` still prints its diagnostic | Unmet | - |\n--- validate ---\n\nSummary: Errors: 0  Warnings: 1\n\nRESULT: PASSED\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"8ec58c","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
