{"toolCallId":"call_c76772fb71684a2093ad147ff331d14e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"+ SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY: Spec doc references, metadata, and handover targets resolve cleanly\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED: Canonical-save root-spec check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED: Canonical-save source-doc check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED: save_lineage is present for the refreshed graph metadata\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED: Packet identity is normalized across continuity, description, and graph surfaces\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS: Description and graph freshness stay within the canonical-save slack window\n+ CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS: Continuity freshness skipped: SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS is not enabled\n    - code:not_opted_in\n+ LINKS_VALID: All wikilinks under the system-spec-kit skill resolve\n\nSummary: Errors: 2  Warnings: 1\n\nRESULT: FAILED\n\nSome of these are recomputable from the repository. Fix them with:\n  node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --apply\n  It rewrites generated metadata (description.json, graph-metadata.json), frontmatter packet\n  pointers and the Spec Folder row, and reports any failure it cannot repair. It never edits\n  other text. Run validate once after it.\n  Optional: run it without --apply first to preview the changes.\nEXIT=2\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a8dd57","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
